# Copy to `.env.local` before building if you want to use a service other than
# Google Gemini. Comma-separated list of origins (scheme + host + port, no path).
#
# This is baked into the bundle at build time and lands in two places at once:
# the Content-Security-Policy `connect-src` in index.html, and the allowlist the
# Settings screen validates against. Anything not listed here cannot be reached,
# no matter what is typed into Settings — that is what stops an injected script
# from posting your API key or your health log to an arbitrary host.
#
# Google's endpoint is always allowed; you never need to list it.
#
# NOTE: never put your API key in here. It would be compiled into the JavaScript
# and shipped inside the APK. The key belongs in Settings, on the device.
#
# VITE_API_ORIGINS=https://openrouter.ai,https://api.groq.com

# Local models (LM Studio, Ollama) — plain http is accepted only for loopback.
# On Android this additionally requires a debug build, because the release
# manifest sets usesCleartextTraffic="false". See README.
# VITE_API_ORIGINS=http://localhost:11434,http://127.0.0.1:1234
